 "notes": [
  "2017 net income and 2018 operating income / EBITDA / net income use the restated ('As Adjusted') comparatives from the following year's releases, so each year follows one definition and its quarters sum to its full year.",
  "2021 (ASU 2020-06): the 2022 releases restated 2021 on a new GAAP basis. Those comparatives start from a GAAP figure that differs from the model, so the extractor skips them (and the add-backs / shares / EPS in the same columns); 2021 stays as originally filed.",
  "'Litigation settlement costs' (2020-21) grouped with IP litigation: the release footnote says they relate to a patent-infringement suit."
 ]
